      "writtenOn": "2021-04-15T15:20:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A timeout of 200ms is almost never useful, because it\u0027s too short to fire reliably on test infra (and thus makes the test flaky) and it\u0027s usually too long to use it often without making the test too slow.\n\nThat said - this looks unused? If so, just remove it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "bdae14734a048c18f35d31e52bd1973c8e3a964f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0cbcba70_784e1f71",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/ConnectivityManagerTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 869,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-15T15:20:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In a recent CL Junyu convinced me that you don\u0027t need to adopt the shell permissions to unregister a callback, even if the callback was filed with the shell permissions.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 868,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 869,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "bdae14734a048c18f35d31e52bd1973c8e3a964f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89ba33f8_25439264",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/ConnectivityManagerTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1627,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-15T15:20:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not just do:\n\n    cb.expectCallback(CallbackEntry.AVAILABLE, ...);\n\n? You might want to use eventuallyExpect to \"skip\" callbacks without failing the test, but that can be a double-edged sword since it will miss cases where the code sends incorrect callbacks. Also, generally nothing happens before onAvailable.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1623,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1627,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "bdae14734a048c18f35d31e52bd1973c8e3a964f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c00d13f9_4246215b",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/ConnectivityManagerTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1840,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-15T15:20:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ConnectivityManagerTest must pass on devices that don\u0027t have wifi. Does this test really require wifi? If so, then you\u0027ll have to arrange to skip it on devices that don\u0027t have wifi, such as:\n\n    assumeTrue(mPackageManager.hasSystemFeature(FEATURE_WIFI));\n\nBonus points for cleaning up all occurrences of code like this:\n\n        if (!mPackageManager.hasSystemFeature(FEATURE_WIFI)) {\n            Log.i(TAG, \"testSocketKeepaliveLimitWifi cannot execute unless device\"\n                    + \" supports WiFi\");\n            return;\n        }\n\nand replacing them with assumeTrue().",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1840,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 1840,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "bdae14734a048c18f35d31e52bd1973c8e3a964f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
